WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.500
A cochlear implant can have up to 22 contacts.

2
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:15.180
Yet in one study of 18 adult implant users, speech scores stopped improving at 8 to

3
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.240
10 channels. So what is a channel?

4
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.920
And why does an electrode in the eye not make a pixel?

5
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:28.070
A contact is hardware on the array, and a channel is a band of frequency

6
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:34.690
information. Clinical maps give higher frequencies to basal contacts and lower ones

7
00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:35.970
to apical contacts.

8
00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:42.130
Neighbouring contacts make overlapping electric fields, called channel interaction.

9
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:46.630
So many contacts do not give as many independent channels.

10
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.110
The plateau depends on array type and placement.

11
00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:56.503
An eye is a camera, so a grid of electrodes should make a grid of dots.

12
00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:03.023
But an electrode on the retina's inner surface sits over ganglion-cell axons running

13
00:01:03.023 --> 00:01:04.203
to the optic disk.

14
00:01:05.243 --> 00:01:10.463
Current excites these axons of passage, and the percept follows the places the axons

15
00:01:10.463 --> 00:01:17.683
serve. Four adults with Argus implants often drew elongated or distorted shapes from

16
00:01:17.683 --> 00:01:21.323
single electrodes, and an axon model accounted for them.

17
00:01:21.903 --> 00:01:25.843
That is a model-supported explanation, not a direct recording.

18
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:32.017
The PRIMAvera study was open-label and single-arm, in adults with geographic

19
00:01:32.017 --> 00:01:39.857
atrophy. 38 people were implanted, 32 were assessed at 12 months, and 26 of those 32

20
00:01:39.857 --> 00:01:43.977
met the endpoint. That is about 81% of those assessed.

21
00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:49.977
Count the six unassessed as not meeting it, and it is about 68% of those implanted.

22
00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:57.030
The endpoint was a gain of at least 0.2 logMAR, measured with the PRIMA glasses.

23
00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:03.630
There, participants could adjust zoom from 1 to 12 times, so a zoomed score measures

24
00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.530
the implant plus a magnifier.

25
00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:12.330
Without zoom or image processing, mean implant resolution was 1.32 logMAR.

26
00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:19.650
20 × 10^1.32 is about 417, so 20/417.

27
00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:24.050
Native resolution and zoom-assisted reading are separate measurements.

28
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:33.120
Serious events belong beside the benefit: 19 participants had 26 serious device- or

29
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.580
procedure-related events.

30
00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.080
So ask what was counted.

31
00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:44.040
Contacts are not channels, electrodes are not pixels, and people assessed are not

32
00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:48.580
people implanted. Native resolution is not zoomed reading.
